WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.518
These days all Americans are told

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.640
go to college!

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.680
A higher education is the

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.572
single best investment.

00:00:07.572 --> 00:00:10.517
But a new book, The Case Against Education

00:00:10.517 --> 00:00:12.059
says this college push

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.480
is a big mistake.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.975
How many thousands of hours

00:00:14.975 --> 00:00:17.070
did you spend in classes studying

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.500
subjects that you never thought about again?

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.540
Economist Bryan Caplan says

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.940
most people who go to college shouldn't.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.740
I learned little in college.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.620
I liked my friends and illegal drinking,

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.900
but I slept through lectures.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.860
At least tuition then was $2,000,

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:35.800
now it's almost $50,000.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.040
People usually just want to talk

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.160
about the tuition, which is a big deal

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.120
but there's also all the years that

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.100
people spend in school

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.720
when they could have been doing something else

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.100
if you just take a look at the faces of

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.530
the students it's obvious that they're bored

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:47.960
and people are there primarily

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.760
in order to get a good job.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.540
Because a diploma is a signaling device

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:53.740
for people with

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.280
no more brains than you have but they have

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.800
one thing you haven't got,

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:58.800
a diploma!

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.220
The con man who was the Wizard of Oz

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.354
hinted at the problem years ago.

00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:04.860
Doctor of Thinkology.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:06.150
Why'd you write this book?

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.547
The Wizard of Oz already made the argument.

00:01:08.547 --> 00:01:10.830
But almost no one seems to believe it.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.500
College graduation has never been more valuable

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.500
than it is today.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.416
Education is my top priority

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.980
and by supporting this budget

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:19.620
you'll make it yours as well.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.980
Meaning taxpayers must pay for it.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:25.100
All the politicians say, go to college.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.100
And there is evidence

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.820
the higher you go, the more money you make.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.531
It's totally true that when people go

00:01:31.531 --> 00:01:33.750
and get more and better and fancier degrees that

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.440
their income generally goes up,

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.860
but the reason why this happening is not really

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.560
that college is pouring tons of job skills into you,

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:41.840
the reason is that it's impressive.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.000
You aren't saying,

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.240
you, individual don't go to college,

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.520
you're saying

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:47.400
we as a country

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.160
are suckers

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:49.923
to push it

00:01:49.923 --> 00:01:51.220
and subsidize it.

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:51.920
Exactly.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:53.860
Just because it is lucrative for an individual

00:01:53.867 --> 00:01:54.810
doesn't mean that's a good

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:55.678
idea for country.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.700
Because when most everyone goes to college,

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.660
that just raises the bar.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:00.960
Imagine that you're at a concert

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.159
and everyone is sitting down and you

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.680
want to see better, what can you do?

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.900
Well you can stand up alright, and of course

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:06.949
then you'll see better.

00:02:06.949 --> 00:02:08.046
Now it does not follow though

00:02:08.046 --> 00:02:09.030
that if everyone stands up

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:10.120
everyone sees better.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:12.020
You just block each other's views.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:13.640
The same thing has happened

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:15.142
in education, says Caplan,

00:02:15.142 --> 00:02:16.740
as more people got degrees,

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:19.600
more employers insisted on degrees.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.499
The result isn't that graduates

00:02:21.499 --> 00:02:22.660
get better jobs,

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:25.459
it's that employers require degrees for

00:02:25.459 --> 00:02:26.980
most every job.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:27.838
There are so many jobs

00:02:27.838 --> 00:02:29.359
where it used to be crazy to think that you

00:02:29.359 --> 00:02:30.497
would need a college degree,

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:31.980
like to be a waiter in a fancy restaurant

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.240
where now it would be very normal.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:36.400
Of course a college education is about more than

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.780
getting a job,

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.280
it's also about learning

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.959
but Caplan says if students really

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:44.600
wanted to learn, they would just do it.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:45.840
If you want to go to Princeton,

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.060
you don't have to apply,

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.940
just move to the town and start attending classes.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:50.380
Nobody does that.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.300
In people's bones they realize

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:54.440
that what really counts is that diploma.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.660
Today that's a taxpayer subsidized diploma

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.560
and when you subsidize something,

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.840
you get more of it.

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.020
More students apply to college,

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:04.980
so schools raise tuition.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.540
Tuition cost has risen

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.520
at triple the rate of inflation.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:09.780
Schools use that money

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:11.540
to attract more students

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:13.083
and more tax money.

00:03:13.083 --> 00:03:16.250
Many compete by advertising luxury.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:18.620
They promote things like lobster dinners,

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:19.860
fancy pools.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.000
Students will come to us and say,

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.260
this is what sealed the deal.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:25.759
Used to be reading, writing, and

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:26.700
arithmetic,

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.320
and well we're now the 4th "r",

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:29.120
recreation.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.520
600 colleges now have rock walls.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:36.920
Give our Tigers spring break every time

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:38.540
they step in

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:40.448
to the Student Recreation Complex.

00:03:40.448 --> 00:03:41.739
This is a public school,

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.040
taxpayers fund that spring break.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.239
We also fund years of study in subjects unlikely

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.960
to help students get jobs,

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:53.080
like social justice,  gender studies, multicultural studies.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:55.760
If we're doing computer science

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:56.820
or electrical engineering,

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:57.640
then you probably

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:00.240
are actually learning a bunch of useful skills,

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.730
but every year we graduate about

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:04.275
twice as many psychology bachelor's degrees

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.680
as we do engineering bachelor's degrees.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.300
Of course there's value in learning psychology,

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.140
philosophy,

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.320
literature,

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:14.600
many employers say they want liberal arts graduates.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.840
It's technology married with liberal arts,

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:19.860
married with the humanities,

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:24.680
that yields us the result that makes our hearts sing.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:27.380
It makes us better, wiser people.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.679
But you can't assume that works.

00:04:28.679 --> 00:04:31.370
How many years of people's lives should

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:32.549
they be made to study stuff

00:04:32.549 --> 00:04:34.700
when the odds that they'll ever appreciate it are

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:36.460
1 in a 100, 1 in a 1000?

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:38.296
Maybe it makes our brains work better?

00:04:38.296 --> 00:04:38.960
It's the kind of thing

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.080
you'd expect teachers say,

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.050
but there's a whole field of people who have

00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:43.240
actually studied this.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.420
Much as they want to believe that you're right

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:46.860
they generally come away

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:48.980
after looking at a lot of evidence and saying,

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:50.300
wow actually

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:51.740
it's wishful thinking.

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:54.100
Although Caplan calls college a scam,

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:54.919
he says it's great

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.600
for a few people.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:57.757
People like him.

00:04:57.757 --> 00:04:59.840
I'm a tenured professor. Your audience may not

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.699
realize how good of a gig this is,

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.320
but a tenured professor cannot be fired

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.658
for almost any reason

00:05:05.658 --> 00:05:07.001
and you get a nice income

00:05:07.001 --> 00:05:09.360
and there almost no demands upon your time.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:11.460
You just have to teach five hours a week?

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:12.760
Well there's people who consider that

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:13.641
a horrible burden.

00:05:13.641 --> 00:05:16.180
That's a scam that we're paying so much money for

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:17.940
people like you to teach you five hours.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.338
Yeah well, I'm a whistleblower.

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:22.320
The bottom line of The Case Against Education:

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:23.220
taxpayers ought to know

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:24.460
that they're getting ripped off.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:26.500
Government has made a tremendous effort

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:27.580
to make education

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:28.555
accessible to everyone.

00:05:28.555 --> 00:05:29.939
I say really what we need to do

00:05:29.939 --> 00:05:31.010
is to go back to a world

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:32.959
where college is not so accessible,

00:05:32.959 --> 00:05:34.908
where it really distinguishes you,

00:05:34.908 --> 00:05:35.900
and in this way,

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:36.960
people are going to be able to

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.180
start their lives years earlier.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:39.540
The wisest solution all things considered

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:41.394
would be if government just got out.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.460
It would be good if government

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:44.100
got out of a lot of things.

